    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Done! The fix passes the `--ci` flag from the root program's options through to the `frai-gate` CLI.\n\n**What was wrong:** The action handler for the `gate` command only received the `args` parameter. When you run `frai gate init --ci`, the root program parses `--ci` as its own option (since it's defined at line 605), and that parsed flag needs to be passed via the `options` parameter.\n\n**How it's fixed:** I added the `options` parameter to the action handler and check if `options.ci` is set. If it is, the `--ci` flag is appended to the arguments before spawning the `frai-gate` CLI. This ensures that `frai gate init --ci` now correctly delegates to `frai-gate init --ci` with the flag included.",
